<span id="S6.SS3.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.92em;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer to RQ3:<span id="S6.SS3.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Each component of EfficientUICoder has a positive impact on results. The
combination of all components brings the best results, which is
much better than using any subset of the three components.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.4. </span>Parameter Study (RQ4)</h3>

<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are three key parameters in EfficientUICoder, the suppress step <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and the decay factor <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> in the Adaptive Duplicate Token Suppression module, and the refinement ratio <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> in the Region-aware Token Refinement module. We sample 100 webpages in Design2Code and 50 webpages in WebCode2M for parameter study.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.4.1. </span>The suppression step <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and decay factor <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct a comprehensive parameter study by setting <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[1,3,5,10]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[1,3,5,10]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[\frac{7}{8},\frac{3}{4},\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{3}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[\frac{7}{8},\frac{3}{4},\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{3}]</annotation></semantics></math>. As shown in Fig. <a href="#S6.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ 6.4.1. The suppression step 𝑠 and decay factor 𝜆 ‣ 6.4. Parameter Study (RQ4) ‣ 6. Experiment Results ‣ EfficientUICoder: Efficient MLLM-based UI Code Generation via Input and Output Token Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S6.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 6.4.1. The suppression step 𝑠 and decay factor 𝜆 ‣ 6.4. Parameter Study (RQ4) ‣ 6. Experiment Results ‣ EfficientUICoder: Efficient MLLM-based UI Code Generation via Input and Output Token Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, EfficientUICoder achieves optimal performance when <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. A suppression step that is too small (<math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;3</annotation></semantics></math>) fails to sufficiently penalize consecutive duplicate tokens, while an excessively large step (<math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;3</annotation></semantics></math>) results in over-penalization. Similarly, when the decay factor <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is too large (close to 1), the logits of redundant code are not effectively reduced, whereas smaller values (<math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\leq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\leq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) achieve similar effects in encouraging non-redundant token selection. Fig. <a href="#S6.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ 6.4.2. The refinement token ratio 𝑟 ‣ 6.4. Parameter Study (RQ4) ‣ 6. Experiment Results ‣ EfficientUICoder: Efficient MLLM-based UI Code Generation via Input and Output Token Compression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> demonstrates that when <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, inference time is significantly reduced to approximately 30 seconds. Our analysis reveals that larger decay factors should be paired with larger penalty steps, while smaller decay factors work better with smaller penalty steps, achieving an optimal balance between penalty intensity and frequency to avoid under- or over-penalization of redundant content.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S6.F8.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel"><img src="2509.12159v1/design2code_block_match_para.png" id="S6.F8.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:110/97;" width="110" height="97" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F8.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S6.F8.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Block Match.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
